                <pb facs="0787" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.154/102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-04T16:00:00-05:00">February 4, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Your despatch No. 77, of January 31, last paragraph. When will investigation
                    be completed? Department desires to act promptly in proposed Chase loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
